# A footprint may be a GeoSPARQL WKT literal, which new data should use (here with the CRS IRI
# GeoSPARQL puts in front of the text), or the plain string existing data uses.
@prefix ex:        <https://hexplain.io/test/footprint-wkt-valid#> .
@prefix xsd:       <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix geosparql: <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#> .
@prefix asref:     <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/spatialref#> .

ex:Scene asref:footprintWKT "<http://www.opengis.net/def/crs/EPSG/0/32611> POLYGON((440720 3751320, 444560 3751320, 444560 3747480, 440720 3747480, 440720 3751320))"^^geosparql:wktLiteral .
ex:Legacy asref:footprintWKT "POLYGON((0 0, 1 0, 1 1, 0 1, 0 0))" .
